WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.288
Module 4: Mosaic
assessments from the Studio.

00:00:03.288 --> 00:00:07.308
You can launch the Mosaic
instruments, developed by Dr.

00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:12.715
Chris Cancialosi, from inside an
engagement and receive the reports there.

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:16.004
The most common is the
Leadership Mosaic 360,

00:00:16.004 --> 00:00:21.192
and its report is the most sensitive
document you'll handle as a coach.

00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:23.092
About thirty-five minutes.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.803
The Assessments tab keeps every assessment
for the engagement in one place,

00:00:28.803 --> 00:00:33.521
and it's private to admins and the
coach unless you share something.

00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:38.239
It holds uploaded reports, validated
questionnaires, assigned forms,

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:42.957
the Mosaic instruments, and, once
there is one, a 360 progress card.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:46.006
To upload a report you already have,

00:00:46.006 --> 00:00:51.225
give it a title and answer one question:
can this assessment be used here?

00:00:51.225 --> 00:00:56.797
For a vendor's report about this coachee,
choose "I have permission to use it".

00:00:56.797 --> 00:00:57.643
Then upload.

00:00:57.643 --> 00:00:59.266
It's marked Coach only.

00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:02.933
Admins and the coach can
open it, the coachee can't,

00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:05.402
until you click Share with coachee.

00:01:05.402 --> 00:01:08.011
Share after you've talked it through.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:13.795
A report read alone at midnight lands very
differently from one read with a coach.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.903
Validated assessments are free,
research-published questionnaires,

00:01:18.903 --> 00:01:20.577
like a well-being index.

00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:23.925
Send one, and the results
come to you privately.

00:01:23.925 --> 00:01:26.435
Share the summary when you're ready.

00:01:26.435 --> 00:01:29.922
The coachee never sees
their item-by-item answers.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:35.641
If they take it again later, a Change since
table shows each dimension going up or

00:01:35.641 --> 00:01:35.990
down.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.872
Higher isn't always better, and small
moves can be ordinary variation.

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:43.453
The table says so, and so should you.

00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:48.105
Five Mosaic instruments can be
launched from an engagement.

00:01:48.105 --> 00:01:51.051
The Leadership Mosaic 360, for one leader.

00:01:51.051 --> 00:01:54.417
The Culture Mosaic, an
organization-wide survey.

00:01:54.417 --> 00:02:00.099
The Culture Progress Monitor, a short
follow-up that re-measures up to three of a

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:01.852
Culture Mosaic's domains.

00:02:01.852 --> 00:02:07.463
Mosaic Signal, a story-based study, only
for organizations with Mosaic included.

00:02:07.463 --> 00:02:12.233
And Culture Dig, a full research
program that runs in its own space.

00:02:12.233 --> 00:02:15.810
SurveyCraft does the survey
work behind the scenes.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:20.930
You use Check progress, and Download
report when there's one to download.

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:23.603
Who pays depends on the license.

00:02:23.603 --> 00:02:28.484
Workspaces with Mosaic instruments
included, like the Mosaic team's own,

00:02:28.484 --> 00:02:29.297
deploy free.

00:02:29.297 --> 00:02:33.839
Other licensed organizations pay
per deployment before it's set up.

00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:36.686
Mosaic Signal is never sold in the Studio.

00:02:36.686 --> 00:02:40.008
For prices, check the
current Mosaic price sheet.

00:02:40.008 --> 00:02:43.669
If you're a Mosaic partner
and your organization pays,

00:02:43.669 --> 00:02:46.245
the dialog asks for your partner code.

00:02:46.245 --> 00:02:48.957
Apply it before you continue to payment.

00:02:48.957 --> 00:02:52.143
And remember: it's for
your own purchases only.

00:02:52.143 --> 00:02:57.702
It works only when you're signed in with
the email the partner portal has for you.

00:02:57.702 --> 00:03:00.617
Never give it to a
client or another coach.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:04.459
Here's the rule that
matters most in this module.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:09.073
A 360 launched from the Studio goes
out the moment you click Deploy.

00:03:09.073 --> 00:03:11.856
There's no draft and no email to approve.

00:03:11.856 --> 00:03:14.028
So have the conversations first.

00:03:14.028 --> 00:03:19.457
Agree the purpose: development, never pay
or promotion, and who sees the report.

00:03:19.457 --> 00:03:23.664
Tell the leader that up to two
bosses are named in the report,

00:03:23.664 --> 00:03:26.990
and make sure each boss
knows before they answer.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:32.283
Explain that peers, direct reports and
others each need three responses to get

00:03:32.283 --> 00:03:35.201
their own section, so
invite five to seven.

00:03:35.201 --> 00:03:40.630
Plan the heads-up note the leader sends
from their own email a day or two before

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:41.716
inviting raters.

00:03:41.716 --> 00:03:44.770
And have them do their
self-assessment first.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:49.860
Avery did all of that with Casey, and
Casey told their boss, Taylor Brooks,

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.692
that Taylor would be named.

00:03:51.692 --> 00:03:53.457
Then Avery clicked Deploy.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:57.833
From the Assessments tab,
choose Leadership Mosaic 360.

00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:02.613
Check the participant's name and
email, which come from the coachee.

00:04:02.613 --> 00:04:05.354
Then set a goal date to close feedback.

00:04:05.354 --> 00:04:07.182
It starts three weeks out.

00:04:07.182 --> 00:04:09.431
It's a target, not a hard close,

00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:14.281
and three days before it the coachee
is emailed their response rates.

00:04:14.281 --> 00:04:16.601
Click Deploy and send invitation.

00:04:16.601 --> 00:04:22.505
You'll get a launch email, then a progress
email every three days, with totals only.

00:04:22.505 --> 00:04:28.058
There's no Close button in the Studio:
a Mosaic administrator closes the 360 in

00:04:28.058 --> 00:04:32.276
SurveyCraft, so agree the end
date with your Mosaic contact.

00:04:32.276 --> 00:04:35.580
Avery deployed Casey's
on the fifth of October.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:41.864
Once the 360 is linked, a progress card
shows how it's going, updated once a day.

00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:43.940
Here's Casey's, nine days in.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.230
The self-assessment is complete.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.878
Three of seven raters have responded.

00:04:48.878 --> 00:04:54.389
The boss has answered, two of four peers,
and none of the two direct reports.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:59.900
Underneath, Things to check flags the
problem: only two direct reports added,

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.837
and they need three responses
to get their own section.

00:05:03.837 --> 00:05:07.701
The card shows counts only,
never a name or an answer.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:12.282
One honest caveat: when a group
is one person, usually the boss,

00:05:12.282 --> 00:05:15.217
the count shows whether they've answered.

00:05:15.217 --> 00:05:18.437
Casey sees the same
counts on their own card.

00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:22.481
It's session two, and Avery
has Casey's card open.

00:05:22.481 --> 00:05:28.442
Decide what Avery should do about the gaps,
and how to answer a question Casey asks.

00:05:28.933 --> 00:05:34.528
When the report is ready, the Mosaic team
can send it from SurveyCraft straight to

00:05:34.528 --> 00:05:35.552
the engagement.

00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:40.055
It only goes where the 360 is
linked, never to a group engagement.

00:05:40.055 --> 00:05:43.535
It lands on the Assessments
tab, marked Coach only,

00:05:43.535 --> 00:05:48.038
and you get an email saying it's
ready, without the file attached.

00:05:48.038 --> 00:05:53.292
Notice the line under it: deleted
automatically on the first of January 2027.

00:05:53.292 --> 00:05:58.819
The report names boss raters, and raters
were told their identifiable feedback is

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:00.184
kept for sixty days.

00:06:00.184 --> 00:06:05.028
So on that date it disappears, for
the coachee too if you've shared it.

00:06:05.028 --> 00:06:10.009
Share it after the debrief, and remind
the leader to keep their own copy.

00:06:10.009 --> 00:06:15.536
Casey's arrived on the second of November,
with the debrief booked for the tenth.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:18.796
Beside the report comes
an AI coach review.

00:06:18.796 --> 00:06:23.744
It's a Word document with three to five
hypotheses to explore in the debrief,

00:06:23.744 --> 00:06:28.435
each with the data for it, the evidence
against it, the pages to look at,

00:06:28.435 --> 00:06:30.041
and questions to test it.

00:06:30.041 --> 00:06:34.025
Treat it as a starting point for
your judgment, not a verdict.

00:06:34.025 --> 00:06:37.109
It's for the engagement's
coach and admins only,

00:06:37.109 --> 00:06:40.836
and the Studio won't let anyone
share it with the coachee.

00:06:40.836 --> 00:06:45.913
Its questions are also added to your
private notes, linked to the next session.

00:06:45.913 --> 00:06:47.840
Be honest about how it's made.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.467
AI writes it from the report's group
scores and comments, with no names.

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:56.965
It's written whatever the coachee
answered about AI in their coaching,

00:06:56.965 --> 00:07:00.113
because it comes from the
360, not your sessions.

00:07:00.113 --> 00:07:02.555
A client can switch these reviews off.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.804
So when you contract with a leader,

00:07:04.804 --> 00:07:08.209
tell them you'll get an
AI-drafted review to prepare,

00:07:08.209 --> 00:07:10.394
and that you'll test it with them.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:15.974
For a Culture Mosaic, you're asked how
many people you'll send the link to.

00:07:15.974 --> 00:07:21.589
Everyone uses the same link, so that number
is how the report shows a true response

00:07:21.589 --> 00:07:21.927
rate.

00:07:21.927 --> 00:07:26.054
Copy the link, share it with
the client, and watch the count.

00:07:26.054 --> 00:07:28.963
Set up report breakdowns
opens SurveyCraft,

00:07:28.963 --> 00:07:32.210
where you choose the groups
the report compares.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.389
With none, it compares
leaders and non-leaders.

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:40.801
The Culture Progress Monitor stays greyed
out until the engagement has a Culture

00:07:40.801 --> 00:07:45.808
Mosaic that's finished setting up, with
at least five completed responses.

00:07:45.808 --> 00:07:49.123
Then you tick one to three
domains to re-measure.

00:07:49.123 --> 00:07:53.114
An older Culture Mosaic has
Community instead of Decisions.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.822
Mosaic Signal is only for
workspaces with Mosaic included,

00:07:57.822 --> 00:08:03.645
up to two hundred and fifty respondents,
and there's no downloadable report yet.

00:08:03.645 --> 00:08:07.648
A Culture Dig launched here
makes you its program lead,

00:08:07.648 --> 00:08:10.778
and the program itself
runs in Culture Dig.

00:08:10.778 --> 00:08:15.073
Check progress shows its phase
and how many stories are in.

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:17.343
Quick check before you move on.

00:08:17.833 --> 00:08:22.644
Here's the Studio 360 checklist:
before you deploy, while it's live,

00:08:22.644 --> 00:08:24.625
and when the report arrives.

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:25.806
To recap.

00:08:25.806 --> 00:08:28.794
Uploads stay Coach only until you share.

00:08:28.794 --> 00:08:31.259
Your partner code is yours alone.

00:08:31.259 --> 00:08:34.920
A Studio 360 goes out
immediately, so talk first.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.534
The card shows counts, never names.

00:08:37.534 --> 00:08:42.539
The report deletes itself, and the
AI coach review is never shared.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:45.378
Next: the view from the admin's chair.

